}

docs {
  # Get Daily Log Configurations
  
  Returns all configuration options for daily logs including:
  - Chronology types (from database: global + house-specific)
  - Statuses
  - Day parts
  - Mood options
  - Wellbeing categories
  - Entry types
  - Safeguarding categories
  
  **Important:** This endpoint automatically syncs global chronologies from config to database.
  
  ## URL Parameters
  - `house` (required): House ID
  
  ## Response Structure
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "All chronology configurations retrieved successfully",
    "data": {
      "configurations": {
        "statuses": ["Pending", "Approved", "Rejected"],
        "day_parts": ["Morning", "Afternoon", "Evening", "Night"],
        "mood_options": ["Happy", "Sad", "Angry", "Calm"],
        "wellbeing_categories": ["Physical wellbeing", "Emotional wellbeing"],
        "entry_types": ["View", "Wish", "Feeling"],
        "safeguarding_categories": ["Physical", "Emotional", "Sexual"]
      },
      "chronology_types": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "name": "No Activity",
          "house_id": null,
          "client_id": null,
          "is_global": true,
          "is_editable": false,
          "created_by": null,
          "updated_by": null,
          "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000000Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000000Z"
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "name": "Health & Well-being",
          "house_id": null,
          "client_id": null,
          "is_global": true,
          "is_editable": false,
          "created_by": null,
          "updated_by": null,
          "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000000Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000000Z"
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "name": "Custom Incident Report",
          "house_id": 1,
          "client_id": 1,
          "is_global": false,
          "is_editable": true,
          "created_by": {
            "id": 42,
            "name": "John Doe"
          },
          "updated_by": {
            "id": 56,
            "name": "Jane Smith"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-01-05T14:30:00.000000Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-01-05T15:45:00.000000Z"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ## Chronology Types Fields
  Each chronology object includes:
  - `id` (integer): Unique chronology identifier
  - `name` (string): Chronology type name
  - `house_id` (integer|null): House ID (null for global chronologies)
  - `client_id` (integer|null): Client ID (null for global chronologies)
  - `is_global` (boolean): True if system-wide chronology, false if house-specific
  - `is_editable` (boolean): True if can be edited/deleted (false for global)
  - `created_by` (object|null): User who created the chronology
    - `id` (integer): User ID
    - `name` (string): User full name
  - `updated_by` (object|null): User who last updated the chronology
    - `id` (integer): User ID
    - `name` (string): User full name
  - `created_at` (timestamp): Creation timestamp
  - `updated_at` (timestamp): Last update timestamp
  
  ## Notes
  - **Global chronologies** (`is_global: true`): System-defined, cannot be edited or deleted
  - **House-specific chronologies** (`is_global: false`): Custom chronologies for the house
  - **Auto-sync**: Global chronologies are automatically synced from config file on each request
  - **Audit trail**: `created_by` and `updated_by` track who made changes (null for global chronologies)
  - **UI guidance**: Use `is_editable` flag to show/hide edit/delete buttons
}
